Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

---

### 1. Before/after every test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

*(You can also use the constructor / `IAsyncDisposable.DisposeAsync` instead.)*

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in the class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before any test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after all tests in this class finish
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

`[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods **must be `static`**.

---

### 3. Once per assembly (before any / after all tests in the assembly)

```csharp
public class WireMockSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // start in-process WireMock server
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // tear down server
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it by attribute.

---

### 4. Once for the entire test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        await Database.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

### Global cross-cutting hooks

Use `[BeforeEvery(...)]` / `[AfterEvery(...)]` to run for *every* test/class/assembly (e.g., logging):

```csharp
public class Logging
{
    [BeforeEvery(Test)]
    public static void Log(TestContext context)
        => Console.WriteLine($"Starting: {context.TestDetails.TestName}");
}
```

---

**Quick reference:**

| Scope | Before | After |
|-------|--------|-------|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` | `[After(Test)]` |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` (static) | `[After(Class)]` (static) |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` (static) | `[After(Assembly)]` (static) |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` (static) | `[After(TestSession)]` (static) |

All hooks can be `async Task` and optionally accept a context parameter and/or `CancellationToken`.
